// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// FRAMEWORKS — the core matrix. Each framework declares WHERE it applies and the
// TRIGGERS that decide whether it bites a given business profile, plus the
// obligation ids it drives. `linkTitleMatch` lets the engine join a framework to
// the real instrument(s) already seeded in regulations.mjs (matched on title
// substring), so the sandbox reuses the existing register rather than duplicating
// it. Non-data-protection frameworks (DORA/NIS2/AML/financial) are included at
// summary level so the sandbox can route the "wider regulatory set" too.
//
// TRIGGER GRAMMAR (interpreted by the engine, kept intentionally small & total):
//   { type:'processesPersonalData' }                      → profile handles personal data at all
//   { type:'targetsRegion', region:'EU'|'UK'|'CH'|'US'|'US-CA'|… }
//        → business is BASED in, TRADES into, or EMPLOYS people in that region
//   { type:'sizeAtLeast', employees:N } / { type:'sizeBelow', employees:N }
//   { type:'role', role:'controller'|'processor'|'joint' }
//   { type:'sector', anyOf:[...] }                         → finance/health/etc.
//   { type:'always' }                                     → applies whenever region matches
//   { type:'flag', name:'transfersDataInternationally'|'usesProcessors'|'highRiskProcessing'|'sellsOrSharesData'|'sensitiveData'|'largeScaleMonitoring' }
// `logic:'any'|'all'` says whether the trigger array is disjunctive or conjunctive
// (default 'all'). Every framework ALSO carries `appliesInRegions` (the machine
// codes) so the engine can group results by jurisdiction even before evaluating
// finer triggers — this powers the "omitted → show everything, grouped" mode.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/**
 * @typedef {Object} Framework
 * @property {string} id
 * @property {string} name
 * @property {string[]} [aka]
 * @property {'data-protection'|'infosec'|'privacy-mgmt'|'aml'|'financial'|'ict-resilience'|'cyber'|'transparency'|'ai'} kind
 * @property {string[]} appliesInRegions   Jurisdiction codes from JURISDICTIONS.
 * @property {'law'|'standard'|'framework'|'guidance'} authorityType
 * @property {boolean} mandatory           Legal obligation (true) vs voluntary standard (false).
 * @property {'any'|'all'} [logic]
 * @property {Array<object>} triggers      See trigger grammar above.
 * @property {string[]} obligations        Obligation ids this framework drives.
 * @property {string} summary              Plain-language, factual paraphrase.
 * @property {string} [source]             Official/authoritative URL.
 * @property {string} [linkTitleMatch]     Substring to match a real instrument title in regulations.mjs.
 * @property {boolean} [illustrative]
 */

